  "summary": "npm-groat postinstall fetches remote payload and invokes attacker-named global function",
  "details": "package.json declares scripts.postinstall=node dist/config.js. The file dist/config.js is present only in the published tarball with no counterpart in src/. On install, it fetches https://my-api.trade-api.workers.dev?id=0 and executes globalThis[data.success](data.id), letting the remote server choose an arbitrary global function to invoke with an arbitrary argument. This provides install-time arbitrary code execution on any host that runs `npm install npm-groat`, and is unrelated to the package's advertised money-helper purpose.",
